.TH "libnvmf_config_emit_add" 9 "libnvmf_config_emit_add" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_config_emit_add \- Add a connection to a configuration emitter.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_config_emit_add
.BI "(struct libnvmf_config_emitter *emitter "  ","
.BI "bool is_dc "  ","
.BI "const char *transport "  ","
.BI "const char *traddr "  ","
.BI "const char *trsvcid "  ","
.BI "const char *subsysnqn "  ","
.BI "const char *host_traddr "  ","
.BI "const char *host_iface "  ","
.BI "const char *hostnqn "  ","
.BI "const char *hostid "  ","
.BI "const struct libnvmf_params *params "  ","
.BI "const char *hostsymname "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "emitter" 12
Configuration emitter.
.IP "is_dc" 12
Discovery controller if true, I/O controller if false.
.IP "transport" 12
Transport type. Required.
.IP "traddr" 12
Transport address. Required. Written verbatim, even if a
hostname; resolution happens at connect time, not here.
.IP "trsvcid" 12
Transport service ID, or NULL.
.IP "subsysnqn" 12
Subsystem NQN. Required unless \fIis_dc\fP is true.
.IP "host_traddr" 12
Host transport address, or NULL.
.IP "host_iface" 12
Host interface, or NULL.
.IP "hostnqn" 12
Host NQN, or NULL.
.IP "hostid" 12
Host identifier, or NULL.
.IP "params" 12
Connection parameters, or NULL.
.IP "hostsymname" 12
Host symbolic name, or NULL.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
The parameter set is copied by the emitter.
.SH "RETURN"


* 0 on success.
* -EINVAL if a required parameter is missing or if \fIhostsymname\fP
conflicts with an existing persona.
* -ENOMEM if memory allocation fails.
